  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 137 PM CDT Sat Oct 31 2026\n\nMonday will be yet another warmer day as clouds thin out further and \nsoutherly flow ramps up ahead of our next cold front scheduled to \narrive early Tuesday morning. Ahead of this front, temperatures will \nwarm into the 80s for most locations outside of the Edwards Plateau \nand western Hill Country. Instability will build ahead of the \napproaching front, but the timing of the front through the overnight \ninto early morning hours Tuesday will probably limit the severe \nthreat. Nevertheless, SPC has introduced a Day 3 Marginal (Level 1 \nof 5) for severe storms over western portions of our area. After the \nline of rain and thunderstorms moves through, we expect cooler and \ndrier weather for the remainder of the week. Cool, crip, comfortable \nmornings in the 40s and 50s along with afternoons in the 70s can be \nexpected. Enjoy!",
